  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sbt/sbt/tarball/v2.0.12",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sbt/sbt/zipball/v2.0.12",
  "body": "## Vulnerability fix for `IO.unzip`\r\n\r\nsbt team received a security report [GHSA-p8jf-532w-4p65](https://github.com/sbt/sbt/security/advisories/GHSA-p8jf-532w-4p65) from [Stas Shevchenko](https://github.com/stasimus) that despite previous attempt to fix it, `IO.unzip` and its variants contain a zip slip vulnerability. sbt 1.13.1 and 2.0.12 fix this bug.\r\n\r\n## updates and bug fixes\r\n\r\n* fix: End the client connection when the channel's write thread stops by @retronym in https://github.com/sbt/sbt/pull/9991\r\n* Update sbtn to 2.1.0-e5346417 in https://github.com/sbt/sbt/pull/9996\r\n* fix: Fix run task by @xuwei-k in https://github.com/sbt/sbt/pull/9963\r\n* IO 1.13.6 by @eed3si9n in https://github.com/sbt/sbt/pull/9989\r\n* Zinc 2.0.5 + IPC Socket 1.8.1 by @eed3si9n in https://github.com/sbt/sbt/pull/9993\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/sbt/sbt/compare/v2.0.11...v2.0.12",
